    "created_at": "2025-04-12T05:46:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-04-12T05:46:34Z",
    "body": "Perhaps a way to add additional elements to a top layer?\n\nInstead of creating new top layers every time a popover or dialog is opened we could do\n\n```\nconst tl = document.createTopLayer()\ndocument.querySelector('dialog').openModal({ layer: tl })\ndocument.querySelector('#toast').showPopover({ layer: tl })\n```\n\nThis would give the user the ability to add to the same top layer multiple elements and use z-index to control them.\n\nHowever there are still edge cases in which multiple top layers might be created and the user need to control their order. Perhaps 3rd party plugins or extensions might cause issues if they decide to adopt the top-layer like intercom, grammarly, nordpass, etc\n\nOne solution can be to pass a \"z-index\" to `createTopLayer`, and top-layers created without it are always showed below the ones created with a z-index > 0",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/whatwg/html/issues/comments/2798506697/reactions",
