    "created_at": "2025-07-29T15:40:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-07-29T15:40:49Z",
    "body": "> I have another related use-case, which is that I need accessibility controls (or, more precisely, the `position: fixed` button that opens the accessibility controls) to still be available even if there's a modal dialog open. It's unfortunate that I'm having to implement layer management, juggling inertness, etc in JS instead of being able to use native platform features due to this constraint.\n\nI'm guessing that `position:fixed` button should actually be within the `<dialog>`, and non-inert that way automatically, or you'll run into problems with AT not being able to get to that button. These are the precise kinds of foot-guns that we're trying to avoid with the current platform behavior.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
