    "updated_at": "2026-01-08T16:18:07Z",
    "body": "This is the biggest hurdle in terms of making the top-layer (and by extension popover and dialog) useable, in my opinion. Large component libraries (like base-ui) don't want to move over until this is solved.\n\nI had some ideas over in https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10370 and @bramus had the idea of [swimlanes](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/10370#issuecomment-2133521439).\n\nThere are now ways, over in JS land (like [this](https://codesandbox.io/p/sandbox/usetoplayerelement-htj44g)), to track what's in the top-layer and move things around to keep them visible and active but they do feel a little hacky.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
