    "created_at": "2026-09-24T12:20:02Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-09-24T12:21:55Z",
    "body": "> this seems like it'd be relevant to web extensions that injects a persistent element as well, does it not?\n\nGenerally we don't design general platform features just for extension use cases, its possible that there's a missing extension API for this sort of UI. Though I'd also suggest that this is a matter of extensions needing to update their code to ensure they're injecting into dialog elements not just the end of the body.\n\nEdit: Well having said the above, in the case of Proton Pass and Passkeys extension handling in general this is very much a missing extension API and the current solution isn't great no matter what (see https://github.com/w3c/webextensions/issues/361)",
